  "storyId": "B-bbaf",
  "name": "convergence-takeover-circuit-breaker",
  "title": "Freeze runaway stories with a convergence + takeover circuit breaker and graduated human ack",
  "description": "B-f458 burned ~14 hours in a non-converging death loop (89 advances, 131:31 review run/pass, 65 lease takeovers) because the framework has soft convergence advisories but no hard brake. Add a circuit breaker that derives FOUR read-only per-story signals — advance-count and review-pass-rate (from story.events and the review ledgers), takeover-frequency (a per-story counter bumped in the existing lease takeover audit write), and repeated-identical-gate-failure (a per-story counter bumped at the existing cli-engine failure write site and reset on a successful advance) — and, on a pathological signature, hard-stops the runaway loop at story_advance. It auto-recovers once so healthy autonomous work is unaffected, and only escalates to a human-ack freeze on re-trip. Scope is death-loop root causes 1 (takeover storm) and 2 (no convergence fuse); the milestone_ledger_set blocker-hint and review_pass_set writer-identity gaps are owned by concurrent stories and excluded.",
